IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca14-accused`

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth of Australia) s 4AA -- what a penalty unit is worth in dollars for the offence I am charged
-- with, read from the Crimes (Amount of a Penalty Unit) Instrument 2026. A module beside ca14-accused.l4 in the same
-- baseline; it IMPORTs that module and changes none of it.
--
-- SEAT: the accused person -- "The offence I am charged with carries a maximum of so many penalty units. How many dollars is
-- that for me?"
--
-- Sources:
--   the Act, compilation C2026C00368, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1914A00012.txt, s 4AA(1), (1A), (3), (8);
--   the Crimes (Amount of a Penalty Unit) Instrument 2026, F2026N00424 (made 15 June 2026, commenced 1 July 2026), as
--   deposited at ../../../crimes-amount-of-a-penalty-unit-instrument-2026/registers/source-bundle/F2026N00424.txt, s 5.
--
-- The indexation formula of s 4AA(3)-(4) is lost from the Act's deposit (NOTES.md finding 14), and is not needed here: the
-- Minister publishes the result (s 4AA(1A)), and the published figure is what this module reads. A failure to publish would
-- not invalidate the indexation (s 4AA(1A)), so for an offence on or after the next indexation day (1 July 2029) the module
-- answers `not covered` rather than carry $364 forward.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA -- what a penalty unit is worth for my offence`

-- s 4AA(1): "penalty unit means the amount of $330 (subject to indexation under subsection (3))."
-- s 4AA(3): "On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in
-- subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula".
-- s 4AA(8): "If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in accordance with subsection (3), the increased
-- amount only applies to offences committed on or after the indexation day."
-- Instrument 2026 s 5: "For the purposes of subsection 4AA(1A) of the Act, the amount of a penalty unit is $364." Its note:
-- the amount "(a) is the result of indexation under subsection 4AA(3) of the Act; and (b) only applies to offences committed on
-- or after 1 July 2026".
-- The $330 itself was substituted by the Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 1) Act 2024 (No. 93, 2024), Sch 3,
-- commencing 7 November 2024 (the Act's endnotes). The earlier amounts, and that Act's application item, are not in the
-- deposited text, so an offence before 7 November 2024 is `not covered`.
DECLARE `What a penalty unit is worth for my offence` IS ONE OF
    `worth in dollars` HAS `the dollar figure` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: my offence was committed before 7 November 2024, and the amount of a penalty unit before the $330 of s 4AA(1) is not in the deposited text`
    `not covered: my offence was committed on or after 1 July 2029, the next indexation day under s 4AA(3), and no instrument publishing that amount is deposited`

GIVETH A DATE
`the first indexation day` MEANS Date 1 7 2026

-- s 4AA(3): "each third 1 July following that day".
GIVETH A DATE
`the next indexation day after 2026` MEANS Date 1 7 2029

-- The day the $330 of s 4AA(1) commenced (Act No. 93, 2024, Sch 3 items 1-3; the Act's endnotes).
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the $330 commenced` MEANS Date 7 11 2024

-- Instrument 2026 s 5.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a penalty unit published for 1 July 2026` MEANS 364

-- s 4AA(1), before indexation.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a penalty unit in s 4AA(1)` MEANS 330

@export My offence against a Commonwealth law has a penalty in penalty units. How many dollars is one penalty unit for my offence?
GIVEN `the day I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed (or is alleged to have been committed)
GIVETH A `What a penalty unit is worth for my offence`
`What is a penalty unit worth for my offence` MEANS
    IF `the day I committed the offence` AT LEAST `the next indexation day after 2026`
    THEN `not covered: my offence was committed on or after 1 July 2029, the next indexation day under s 4AA(3), and no instrument publishing that amount is deposited`
    ELSE IF `the day I committed the offence` AT LEAST `the first indexation day`
         THEN `worth in dollars` `the amount of a penalty unit published for 1 July 2026`
         ELSE IF `the day I committed the offence` AT LEAST `the day the $330 commenced`
              THEN `worth in dollars` `the amount of a penalty unit in s 4AA(1)`
              ELSE `not covered: my offence was committed before 7 November 2024, and the amount of a penalty unit before the $330 of s 4AA(1) is not in the deposited text`

-- A number of penalty units, in dollars at the value that applies to the offence.
GIVEN `the number of penalty units` IS A NUMBER
      `the value` IS A `What a penalty unit is worth for my offence`
GIVETH A `What a penalty unit is worth for my offence`
`so many penalty units at` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the value`
    WHEN `worth in dollars` `d` THEN `worth in dollars` (`the number of penalty units` TIMES `d`)
    OTHERWISE `the value`

@export The maximum penalty for my offence is stated in penalty units. What is that in dollars?
GIVEN `the day I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed (or is alleged to have been committed)
      `the maximum penalty in penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum penalty for the offence, in penalty units, as the law creating the offence states it
GIVETH A `What a penalty unit is worth for my offence`
`What is my maximum penalty in dollars` MEANS
    `so many penalty units at` `the maximum penalty in penalty units` (`What is a penalty unit worth for my offence` `the day I committed the offence`)

-- s 20(5) gives the most a s 20 recognizance can make me pay in penalty units (ca14-accused.l4); here it is in dollars.
@export If I am released on a s 20 recognizance without being sentenced, what is the most the court can make me pay as a penalty, in dollars?
GIVEN `the day I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day you committed the offence you were convicted of
      `my offence is punishable by a fine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence you were convicted of is punishable by a fine
      `the maximum fine in penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum fine, in penalty units, the court could impose on you for the offence (ignored if it is not punishable by a fine)
      `I am in a court of summary jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court that convicted you is a court of summary jurisdiction (a local or magistrates court), rather than a higher court
GIVETH A `What a penalty unit is worth for my offence`
`The most a s 20 recognizance can make me pay in dollars` MEANS
    `so many penalty units at`
        (`The most a s 20 recognizance can make me pay in penalty units` `my offence is punishable by a fine` `the maximum fine in penalty units` `I am in a court of summary jurisdiction`)
        (`What is a penalty unit worth for my offence` `the day I committed the offence`)
